                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Tractor Ball finds its home in a long forgotten corner of the internet. It wears it's troll face with conviction, not oblivious to the passing of time but artfully obstinate in it's refusal to except it. \nAt first glance what's ostensibly a mere \"Rocket League Clone\" is actually a perfectly crafted satire, unabashedly turning away players with it's clunky gameplay in favour of achieving it's delicate social commentary.\nTractor Ball isn't a clunky, derivitive mess, it's a work of art often smarter than it's audience which it amazingly achieves without seeming condescending. Tractor Ball is smart because it makes us think that it's stupid and it's within that subtle manipulation that it masterfully gets the best of it's audience, having a small player base is in a sense the aim of Tractor Ball and as such, against all common criteria of video game critique Tractor Ball has won.\n\nTractor Ball is the 10/10 experience you'll probably never experience because Tractor Ball doesn't want you too, even if you do it's avant-garde approach to game design and audience retention will ensure you don't want to stick around.",
